</style></head><body><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini Apps<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted Fix all of what chatgpt was to lazy to thanks bossThis first block of code is closest to what

want but need the added functionality discussed below&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no&quot;&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Spritz Reader&lt;/title&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
:root {
  --bg: #0b0b0b;
  --fg: #ffffff;
  --muted: #8a8a8a;
  --accent: #ff3b3b;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100vh;
  overflow: hidden;
  touch-action: manipulation;
}

textarea {
  width: 94%;
  height: 120px;
  margin-top: 10px;
  padding: 12px;
  font-size: 15px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  border: none;
  resize: none;
}

.controls {
  width: 94%;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  margin: 10px 0;
}

.controls label {
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--muted);
}

input[type=&quot;range&quot;] {
  flex: 1;
}

.wpm {
  width: 60px;
  text-align: right;
  font-weight: 600;
}

button {
  background: #1c1c1c;
  color: #fff;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 8px 12px;
  font-size: 16px;
}

.hint {
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--muted);
  margin-bottom: 4px;
}

.reader {
  flex: 1;
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  user-select: none;
}

.word {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  font-size: 56px;
}

.left {
  min-width: 120px;
  text-align: right;
}

.orp {
  color: var(--accent);
  padding: 0 4px;
}

.right {
  min-width: 120px;
  text-align: left;
}

.context {
  margin-top: 16px;
  font-size: 20px;
  color: var(--muted);
  max-width: 90%;
  text-align: center;
}

.progress-container {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 6px;
  background: #222;
}

.progress {
  height: 100%;
  width: 0%;
  background: var(--accent);
}
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;

&lt;body&gt;

&lt;textarea id=&quot;textInput&quot;&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;controls&quot;&gt;
  &lt;label&gt;WPM&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;wpmSlider&quot; min=&quot;100&quot; max=&quot;1500&quot; step=&quot;5&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;wpm&quot; id=&quot;wpmValue&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;button onclick=&quot;toggleFullscreen()&quot;&gt;⛶&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;hint&quot;&gt;Tap = play / pause • Double tap = restart&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;reader&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div id=&quot;word&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;context&quot; id=&quot;context&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;progress-container&quot;&gt;
  &lt;div class=&quot;progress&quot; id=&quot;progress&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
/* =========================
   DEFAULT TEXT (SAFE)
========================= */
const DEFAULT_TEXT = `Welcome to the Spritz-style speed reader.

This tool presents one word at a time at a fixed focal point, minimizing eye movement and improving reading speed.

Tap once to start or pause.
Double tap to restart from the beginning.
Adjust the slider to change speed in real time.

Your preferred reading speed is saved automatically.`;

const textInput = document.getElementById(&quot;textInput&quot;);
textInput.value = DEFAULT_TEXT;

let defaultTextActive = true;

textInput.addEventListener(&quot;focus&quot;, () =&gt; {
  if (defaultTextActive) {
    textInput.value = &quot;&quot;;
    defaultTextActive = false;
  }
});

/* =========================
   STATE
========================= */
let words = [];
let index = 0;
let timer = null;
let state = &quot;IDLE&quot;;
let lastTap = 0;
let wpm = 555;

/* =========================
   ELEMENTS
========================= */
const wordEl = document.getElementById(&quot;word&quot;);
const contextEl = document.getElementById(&quot;context&quot;);
const progress = document.getElementById(&quot;progress&quot;);
const slider = document.getElementById(&quot;wpmSlider&quot;);
const wpmValue = document.getElementById(&quot;wpmValue&quot;);

/* =========================
   INIT
========================= */
const savedWpm = localStorage.getItem(&quot;wpm&quot;);
if (savedWpm) wpm = Number(savedWpm);

slider.value = wpm;
wpmValue.textContent = wpm;

slider.addEventListener(&quot;input&quot;, () =&gt; {
  wpm = Number(slider.value);
  wpmValue.textContent = wpm;
  localStorage.setItem(&quot;wpm&quot;, wpm);
});

/* =========================
   TEXT LOAD
========================= */
function loadText() {
  words = textInput.value.trim().split(/\s+/);
  index = 0;
  progress.style.width = &quot;0%&quot;;
}

/* =========================
   ORP
========================= */
function getORPIndex(word) {
  if (word.length &lt;= 1) return 0;
  if (word.length &lt;= 5) return 1;
  if (word.length &lt;= 9) return 2;
  return 3;
}

function formatWord(word) {
  const i = getORPIndex(word);
  return `
    &lt;div class=&quot;word&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;left&quot;&gt;${word.slice(0, i)}&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;orp&quot;&gt;${word[i] || &quot;&quot;}&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;right&quot;&gt;${word.slice(i + 1)}&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  `;
}

/* =========================
   TIMING
========================= */
function getDelay(word) {
  let delay = 60000 / wpm;
  if (/[,.]/.test(word)) delay *= 1.5;
  if (/[!?]/.test(word)) delay *= 2;
  return delay;
}

/* =========================
   LOOP
========================= */
function tick() {
  if (index &gt;= words.length) {
    pause();
    return;
  }

  const currentWord = words[index];
  wordEl.innerHTML = formatWord(currentWord);
  contextEl.textContent = &quot;&quot;;
  progress.style.width = ((index + 1) / words.length) * 100 + &quot;%&quot;;
  index++;

  timer = setTimeout(tick, getDelay(currentWord));
}

/* =========================
   CONTROLS
========================= */
function start() {
  if (state === &quot;IDLE&quot;) loadText();
  if (!words.length) return;

  contextEl.textContent = &quot;&quot;;
  state = &quot;RUNNING&quot;;
  tick();
}

function pause() {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  state = &quot;PAUSED&quot;;

  const remaining = words.slice(index).join(&quot; &quot;);
  contextEl.textContent = remaining;
}

function restart() {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  loadText();
  state = &quot;IDLE&quot;;
  start();
}

/* =========================
   TAP HANDLING
========================= */
document.body.addEventListener(&quot;click&quot;, () =&gt; {
  const now = Date.now();

  if (now - lastTap &lt; 300) {
    restart();
  } else {
    state === &quot;RUNNING&quot; ? pause() : start();
  }

  lastTap = now;
});

/* =========================
   FULLSCREEN
========================= */
function toggleFullscreen() {
  if (!document.fullscreenElement) {
    document.documentElement.requestFullscreen();
  } else {
    document.exitFullscreen();
  }
}
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;You’re still thinking like someone who ships real products 👍
What you’re asking for now is exactly what a serious long-form reader needs.

Below is a fully integrated, production-grade, single-file HTML that adds both requested features without introducing UX hazards.


---

✅ What’s added (precisely)

1. Pre-context + Post-context when paused

When paused:

The focused word stays identical (size, ORP, position)

A small, grey pre-context (words before the focus) appears above

A small, grey post-context (words after the focus) appears below

Context is limited to the current paragraph window, not the whole document

On resume → both contexts disappear instantly


This mirrors high-end RSVP / Spritz readers and preserves eye anchoring.


---

2. Persistent reading state (book-safe)

Saved to localStorage:

✅ User text (never overwritten)

✅ Current word index

✅ WPM

✅ Automatically restored on reload


Result:

&gt; Someone can paste a book, close the browser, reopen later, and continue exactly where they left off.



No accidental resets. No surprise overwrites.


---

3. Demo text safety (still correct)

Demo text loads only if no saved user text exists

Clicking textarea clears only demo text

User text is never auto-cleared

Saved text always wins over demo text



---

📄 Final production HTML

Save as: spritz-reader.html

&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;
&lt;head&gt;
&lt;meta charset=&quot;UTF-8&quot;&gt;
&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no&quot;&gt;
&lt;title&gt;Spritz Reader&lt;/title&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
