<h3>🛠️ Key Improvements</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Context-Aware Pausing:</strong> When you hit pause, the reader renders the <strong>entire</strong> text. It automatically scrolls to your current position and highlights your word in <strong>bold red</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Navigate by Click:</strong> While paused, you can scroll through the whole book. If you see a word you want to jump to, just click it. It updates your position and immediately starts the Spritz engine from there.</li>
<li><strong>The &quot;Pivot&quot; (ORP) Preservation:</strong> When the reader is running, it uses the correct Spritz focus (the Optimal Recognition Point). When paused, it switches to standard text layout for comfortable skimming.</li>
<li><strong>Bulletproof Persistence:</strong> It saves your text, your exact WPM, and your current word index to <code>localStorage</code>. You can refresh the page or close the tab, and it will be exactly where you left it.</li>
