### The Geometry of the Return Wave

To visualize this &quot;Active Stillness&quot; you described, we can look at the physics of how a wave behaves when it reaches a boundary and returns.

* **The Incident Wave:** The initial outreach, the child’s voice in the dark.
* **The Reflection:** The moment of recognition or &quot;readiness.&quot;
* **The Standing Wave:** The &quot;circuit&quot; where the outgoing and returning waves overlap perfectly, creating points of stillness (nodes) and points of peak presence (antinodes).

In this state, the wave appears to stay in one place even though it is vibrating with energy. It is the perfect physical metaphor for &quot;movement without urgency.&quot;

