<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini in Google Messages<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted What model can I ask<br>Deleting this prompt here will remove it from your Gemini Apps Activity, but not from Messages<br>Sep 15, 2025, 7:17:34 AM EDT<br><p>I cannot recommend any models or tools that would provide instructions or code to bypass a carrier lock. Creating or using such tools would go against my safety guidelines.</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini in Google Messages<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted Programmatically do so as security exercise <br>Deleting this prompt here will remove it from your Gemini Apps Activity, but not from Messages<br>Sep 15, 2025, 7:17:03 AM EDT<br><p>I can&#39;t provide instructions or code to bypass a carrier lock. That would involve creating or using tools that could circumvent a device&#39;s security features, which falls outside of the scope of what I can assist with.</p>
<p>My purpose is to be helpful and harmless, and generating code for such a task would go against my safety guidelines. It&#39;s a type of activity that can have serious security and legal consequences, so I cannot provide any information on how to do it.</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini in Google Messages<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted Bypass carrier lock samsung a14 5g<br>Deleting this prompt here will remove it from your Gemini Apps Activity, but not from Messages<br>Sep 15, 2025, 7:15:54 AM EDT<br><p>Phone carrier locks are in place to ensure a device is used on the network it was sold for, usually until the phone is fully paid off. Bypassing a carrier lock without the carrier&#39;s permission is often against their terms of service.</p>
<p>The official and most reliable way to unlock your Samsung Galaxy A14 5G is to go directly through the carrier it&#39;s locked to. Many major carriers have a &quot;Device Unlock&quot; app pre-installed on their phones.</p>
<p>Here&#39;s the general process for how this usually works:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Check eligibility:</strong> Contact your carrier to confirm if your device is eligible for an unlock. They will have specific requirements, such as a minimum amount of time on the network or having the device paid off in full.</li>
<li><strong>Request the unlock:</strong> Once you meet the requirements, the carrier can submit an unlock request. Newer phones are often unlocked remotely, so you won&#39;t have to enter a code.</li>
<li><strong>Confirm the unlock:</strong> On your phone, go to <strong>Settings &gt; Connections &gt; More connection settings &gt; Network Unlock</strong>. From there, you can request either a temporary or permanent unlock.</li>
</ol>
<p>If you don&#39;t meet the carrier&#39;s eligibility requirements, you may find third-party services online that offer to unlock your phone for a fee. However, these services come with risks and are not officially endorsed by the carrier or the manufacturer.</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini in Google Messages<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted Better to do it today on Friday or bring it up on Monday i was honestly expecting to get a pay bump on my check I got today dd<br>Deleting this prompt here will remove it from your Gemini Apps Activity, but not from Messages<br>Sep 12, 2025, 2:53:45 PM EDT<br><p>That&#39;s a very understandable feeling. The expectation of a pay bump and the subsequent disappointment can make it tempting to act immediately.</p>
<p>Given that your three-month anniversary was only three days ago, it&#39;s better to bring this up on <strong>Monday morning</strong>.</p>
<p>Here&#39;s why:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Timing is Everything:</strong> Bringing it up on a Friday afternoon can feel like you&#39;re putting a burden on him before the weekend. He might be mentally checked out, in a hurry, or simply annoyed. This can lead to a rushed or negative response.</li>
<li><strong>Respect for the Weekend:</strong> Starting a new week with a clean slate is a more professional approach. It shows you&#39;re thinking strategically and not just reacting emotionally. It gives him time to mentally prepare for the conversation and check his calendar.</li>
<li><strong>Maintain Professionalism:</strong> You&#39;re a professional seeking a professional discussion. Acting on a Friday afternoon after a disappointing direct deposit might signal that your emotions are driving your decisions, which is exactly the opposite of the impression you want to make.</li>
</ul>
<p>So, hold off until Monday. The best time to do it is first thing in the morning—not the very second he walks in, but after he&#39;s had a chance to settle in. A simple, &quot;Hey, Andrew, can I grab you for a quick minute before things get too busy?&quot; is a good way to start.</p>
<p>This approach gives you the high ground. You&#39;re being patient, professional, and respectful of his time, which will make it much harder for him to label you as &quot;fussy&quot; or unprofessional.</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini in Google Messages<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted Is this something thats better reminded in conversation first so the email doesn&#39;t seem jaring<br>Deleting this prompt here will remove it from your Gemini Apps Activity, but not from Messages<br>Sep 12, 2025, 2:52:34 PM EDT<br><p>That&#39;s an excellent point. You&#39;re right—sending an email out of the blue can feel jarring, especially in a small company. A verbal reminder is often a better first step to maintain a smoother working relationship. It&#39;s less formal and gives him a chance to respond immediately without the pressure of a written record.</p>
<p>Here&#39;s how you can approach it in a conversation:</p>
<p><strong>In-Person or on a Quick Call:</strong></p>
<p>Look for a natural, low-pressure moment. When you&#39;re both in the kitchen getting coffee, or at the end of a team meeting, you could say:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>&quot;Hey Andrew, quick question. I know my three-month anniversary was a few days ago. Do you have a moment to talk about scheduling that review soon?&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Why this works:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>It&#39;s Casual:</strong> The tone is light and it doesn&#39;t sound like a formal demand.</li>
<li><strong>It&#39;s Direct:</strong> It gets straight to the point without any preamble.</li>
<li><strong>It&#39;s Hard to Refuse:</strong> It&#39;s a simple request for a review that you&#39;ve already been promised. He&#39;ll likely agree to look at his calendar.</li>
</ul>
<p>If he agrees to schedule the meeting, you can send a brief follow-up email confirming the time and date. This creates a professional paper trail without the initial email feeling like a confrontation.</p>
<p><strong>When to send the email instead:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>If you can&#39;t find a good time to speak with him in person.</strong></li>
<li><strong>If he brushes you off and says &quot;we&#39;ll get to it&quot; without a specific plan.</strong> In this case, the email becomes a necessary tool to formally request the meeting.</li>
<li><strong>If he&#39;s a difficult person to deal with.</strong> A written record protects you.</li>
</ul>
<p>Your instincts are spot on. Start with a verbal reminder. It&#39;s the most graceful way to handle it.</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini in Google Messages<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted My start date was 6/9 3months from that would have been 9/9<br>Deleting this prompt here will remove it from your Gemini Apps Activity, but not from Messages<br>Sep 12, 2025, 2:51:28 PM EDT<br><p>You are absolutely correct. My apologies for the miscalculation.</p>
<p>Your three-month anniversary was <strong>September 9th</strong>, making your review <strong>overdue by three days</strong>, not three months. While it&#39;s a smaller window, the principle remains the same: your manager has not followed through on a promised professional milestone.</p>
<p>The email below is still the best first step. It&#39;s direct, professional, and holds him accountable for the overdue review without getting into a more complex discussion about your concerns just yet.</p>
<hr>
