<p>Let&#39;s break down why it&#39;s the strongest choice and how to prepare for the conversation.</p>
<h3>The Best Email: The First Draft</h3>
<p>The first email strikes the perfect balance. It&#39;s honest without being aggressive, and it directly connects your performance to the systemic issues of <strong>overwork and under-compensation.</strong></p>
<ul>
