{&quot;contentMetadata&quot;:{&quot;tag&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;toolAttribution&quot;:{&quot;displayName&quot;:&quot;Device Setting Tool&quot;,&quot;logoUri&quot;:&quot;https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg&quot;,&quot;toolName&quot;:&quot;device_setting&quot;}}}</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini Apps<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted set screen timeout to 15 minutes<br>Sep 2, 2025, 8:02:24 PM EDT<br><p>I cannot directly set the screen timeout. However, I can open the display settings for you, where you can adjust it. Would you like me to do that?</p>
<br></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1 mdl-typography--text-right"></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-typography--caption"><b>Products:</b><br>&emsp;Gemini Apps<br><b>Why is this here?</b><br>&emsp;This activity was saved to your Google Account because the following settings were on:&nbsp;Gemini Apps Activity.&nbsp;You can control these settings &nbsp;<a href="https://myaccount.google.com/activitycontrols">here</a>.</div></div></div><div class="outer-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col mdl-shadow--2dp"><div class="mdl-grid"><div class="header-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--12-col"><p class="mdl-typography--title">Gemini Apps<br></p></div><div class="content-cell mdl-cell mdl-cell--6-col mdl-typography--body-1">Prompted Eidetic<br>Sep 2, 2025, 7:59:00 PM EDT<br><p>Eidetic memory, often referred to as &quot;photographic memory,&quot; is the ability to recall an image from memory with high precision and vividness, as if it were still being perceived. The term comes from the Greek word <em>eidetikos</em>, which means &quot;pertaining to images.&quot;</p>
<p>Here are some key characteristics of eidetic memory:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Vividness:</strong> The memory is so clear and detailed that the person can describe it with great accuracy.</li>
<li><strong>Transient:</strong> This ability is typically short-term, lasting only for a brief period after seeing the image.</li>
<li><strong>Distinct from photographic memory:</strong> While often used interchangeably, some researchers distinguish between the two. Eidetic memory is more focused on the visual &quot;afterimage&quot; that a person can &quot;see&quot; in their mind&#39;s eye, while photographic memory may be used to describe a broader, and scientifically debated, ability to recall detailed information like pages of text or numbers.</li>
<li><strong>Mostly found in children:</strong> Eidetic memory is a rare phenomenon that is most commonly observed in young children and tends to fade as they age. It&#39;s believed that as the brain develops and relies more on language and abstract thought, the ability for this kind of vivid, visual recall diminishes.</li>
<li><strong>No mnemonics:</strong> True eidetic memory does not rely on mnemonic devices, expert talent, or other cognitive strategies. The recall is a natural, almost automatic, process.</li>
</ul>
<p>It is important to note that the existence of a true &quot;photographic&quot; memory—the ability to permanently store and recall entire pages of text or numbers with perfect accuracy—is highly debated in the scientific community and has not been conclusively proven.</p>
